Sat Sep 26 18:11:48 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 0.1.15 (upstream assigned no CVE ids and shipped no
  advisory):
  * Memory-safety sweep on untrusted input: AprilTag RLE run-buffer
    heap overflow on 1-pixel stripes, kornia-io decoder pixel cap
    and GStreamer pipeline injection, imgproc out-of-bounds in
    warp/remap/resize, numpy binding misuse, C++ FFI null/overflow
    checks.
  * OpenCV-parity image processing on CPU (NEON) and CUDA: Canny,
    median and bilateral blur, CLAHE, connected components,
    histogram, Gaussian pyramids, SIFT, CUDA remap, Laplacian,
    integral image.
  * New kornia-calib crate for multi-camera extrinsic calibration;
    bundle adjustment gains intrinsics, priors and Huber-robust
    PnP.
  * Tensors and images dispatch on CPU/CUDA residency, with unified
    and pinned write-combined allocators plus zero-copy host
    buffers.
  * Breaking Rust API: unchecked accessors are now unsafe, several
    permutation and rectification entry points return Result.
  * RVL reaches 5.7x compression; histogram, colour-check and
    pyramid APIs filled in on the Python side.
- Switch Source0 to the release tag: upstream removed --sdist from
  its release workflow in 0.1.15 ("not self-contained"), so no PyPI
  sdist exists from this version on. The tag keeps pyproject.toml
  in the binding crate, so the PEP 517 build now runs from
  kornia-py/.
- Require rust >= 1.89, upstream's new floor.

